<title>UK: NWE gasoline softens in line with futures.</title>
<headline>NWE gasoline softens in line with futures.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>NWE gasoline was softer on Friday after recent falls on IPE and NYMEX futures dragged numbers lower, traders said.</p>
<p>Eurograde barges traded at $201 and $201.75 fob ARA while March swaps were pegged slower to $203.</p>
<p>Material remains relatively tight in northwest Europe and the Med in the prompt period.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 8167</p>
